```
hitrate() {
  docker compose exec redis redis-cli INFO stats | tr -d '\r' | awk -F: '
    /keyspace_hits/ {h=$2} /keyspace_misses/ {m=$2}
    END { printf "hits=%d misses=%d hit rate=%.1f%%\n", h, m, (h+m) ? 100*h/(h+m) : 0 }'
}
```

### Run A: baseline (warm cache, skewed traffic)
```
mkdir -p results
k6 run loadtest/redirect.js > /dev/null                 # warm-up run, result ignored
docker compose exec redis redis-cli CONFIG RESETSTAT
k6 run --summary-export=results/A-baseline.json loadtest/redirect.js
hitrate
```

### Run B: cold cache
```
docker compose exec redis redis-cli FLUSHALL            # empty the cache
docker compose exec redis redis-cli CONFIG RESETSTAT
k6 run --summary-export=results/B-cold.json loadtest/redirect.js
hitrate
```

### Run C: Redis goes down mid-test
```
# terminal 2
docker compose exec redis redis-cli CONFIG RESETSTAT
k6 run --summary-export=results/C-redis-down.json loadtest/redirect.js

# terminal 3: wait 40 seconds, then stop Redis
sleep 40 && docker compose stop redis
```

### Run D: uniform traffic (no popular links)
```
docker compose exec redis redis-cli FLUSHALL
k6 run -e SKEW=1 loadtest/redirect.js > /dev/null      # warm-up with the same traffic shape
docker compose exec redis redis-cli CONFIG RESETSTAT
k6 run -e SKEW=1 --summary-export=results/D-uniform.json loadtest/redirect.js
hitrate
```
